# Sign boards

A scene can be a wooden sign with painted letters instead of floating text. A
sign is a real object in the world: it can be read from across the street, and
it stays through restarts like any scene.

Sign boards need the **Poggy Scene Props** resource (`poggy_scene_props`),
started **before** Poggy Scene. Without it everything else works as before and
the Scene Editor simply offers no sign.

## Putting up a sign

Type `/scene` and click **Sign board** at the top of the editor. The sign stands
in front of you as you make it and changes as you go.

1. **Board:** step through the shapes with ◄ ►: Plank board, Crowned board, Oval, Tall board, or an Arrow pointing right or left.
2. **Board colour:** Light (cream paint) or Dark (stained timber).
3. **Lettering:** Rocks (tall, narrow) or Serif (an old printed face).
4. **Words run:** Across, or Down (letters stacked, for the Tall board).
5. Type the words in the box. **Enter** starts a new line (a new column when the words run down).
6. To change part of the words, **select it**, then pick a size (Large, Medium, Small) or click a paint.
   Pick a size or paint with nothing selected and what you type next uses it.
7. Move and turn it with the sliders, at any time.
8. Click **✓ Place**.

## Optional extras

None of these is needed; each starts at **None**.

| Extra | What it is |
|---|---|
| **Symbols** | Thirty-five painted emblems (a star, a horseshoe, pointing hands, a steer skull, crossed pistols, tools and trades, cards and dice, a lawman's badge and many more) and three flourishes (a rule with a diamond, scrolls, a star with dots). Click one to write it in where you are typing. It behaves like a letter: it takes the size and paint in use, you can select it and change either, and it can sit beside words or on a line of its own. |
| **Painted border** | A sign painter's line just inside the frame, in any paint. |
| **Mount** | A hanging iron bracket with chains, a single post, or two posts. The posts reach about two metres below the sign: lower the sign until they meet the ground. |
| **Light** | A lamp over the sign, or bulbs round its frame. After dark it lights the sign's face. |
| **Sides** | **Both** puts the same words on the back, for a sign that hangs out over a street. The mount and the lamp are shared; bulbs go round both faces. A sign on a single post has the post behind it, so use the bracket or two posts for a sign read from both sides. |

## The paints

Dark, Light, Red, Green, Blue, Cyan, Magenta and Yellow. Plain typing is Dark
on a light board and Light on a dark one. Any paint can go on any board, and a
line can mix paints and sizes.

## Placing it

| Slider | What it does |
|---|---|
| Left / right, Near / far, Down / up | Moves the sign from where it appeared, as you were standing. |
| Turn | Which way it faces. |
| Tilt | Leans the top towards you or away. |
| Lean | Tips it to one side. |

Drag a slider, scroll on it (hold **Shift** for bigger steps), or type a number.
Click and hold outside the panel to look around.

## Room on the board

Nothing you type is refused for its size. The words are centred on the board,
and words that are too long or too many simply run past the frame, so you can
see it and decide. The line under the box shows how much room is used and says
**runs past the board** when they do.

Two sliders under the box set how the words sit:

| Slider | What it does |
|---|---|
| Line spacing | The gap between lines (between columns when the words run down), in centimetres. It can go below zero to close lines up. |
| Words up / down | Moves all the words up or down on the board, in centimetres. Use it to make room for a symbol at the top, or to sit the words in the crown of the Crowned board. |

The only limits are the number of letters and symbols on one sign (an owner
setting, 60 by default) and fourteen lines.

| Board | Room for words |
|---|---|
| Plank board | 1.34 m wide, 0.46 m high |
| Crowned board | 1.32 m wide, 0.46 m high |
| Oval | 1.00 m wide, 0.44 m high |
| Tall board | 0.34 m wide, 1.36 m high |
| Arrow | 1.00 m wide, 0.32 m high |

Letter heights: Rocks 18, 11 and 6 cm; Serif 13, 8.5 and 5 cm. Emblems are 18,
12 and 7 cm tall.

Signs are **capitals**, the numbers, and `& . , ' ! ? - $ : / #`. Anything else
is left out. In Rocks the `&` is drawn as a plus sign.

## Changing or removing a sign

Stand close to a sign you put up yourself and press **4**. The Scene Editor opens on it, where it is:

- change the words, the board or anything else, move it if you like, and click **✓ Save**;
- or click **Remove** (twice, to be sure) to take it down;
- **Cancel** leaves it as it was.

The admin group can do the same to anyone's sign. The remove jobs cannot change someone else's sign,
but pressing 4 beside it removes it. Staff can also delete signs from **/poggy** → **Poggy Scene** →
**Scenes**.

## Settings

All under **/poggy** → **Poggy Scene**.

| Setting | Default | What it does |
|---|---|---|
| Sign boards | on | Switches the whole feature on or off. |
| Signs are solid | on | A placed sign and its posts are solid. Off lets players walk through them. |
| Signs light up after dark | on | A sign with a lamp or bulbs lights its own face at night. |
| Fetch sign props in the background | on | The first sign a player sees or makes appears at once. |
| Most letters and symbols on a sign | 60 | Each is its own prop. Lower keeps busy streets light. |
| Sign view distance | 40 m | Signs further away than this are not drawn. |
| Most signs shown at once | 12 | Each player sees the nearest ones only. |
| Jobs that may put up signs | empty | Empty means everyone who can place a scene. |
| Most signs per character | 5 | 0 means no limit. The admin group is not limited. |

A placed sign and its posts are solid. If signs get used to block doorways, turn
**Signs are solid** off and players walk through them instead; staff can also
remove any sign.
